  "instructions": [
    "Preheat an oven to 375°F (190°C).",
    "Line a baking sheet with parchment paper.",
    "Spread the dried white corn evenly onto the prepared baking sheet.",
    "Place the binchotan charcoal sheet on top of the corn and fold the parchment paper to create a makeshift smoker.",
    "Place the baking sheet in the oven and smoke for 15 minutes.",
    "Remove the baking sheet from the oven and drizzle with olive oil, lemon juice, and orange juice.",
    "Sprinkle salt, black pepper, garlic powder, and paprika over the corn mixture.",
    "Bake for an additional 10 minutes, or until the corn is lightly toasted.",
    "Remove the baking sheet from the oven and sprinkle with Monterey Jack cheese.",
    "Return the baking sheet to the oven and bake until the cheese is melted and bubbly.",
    "Sprinkle chopped cilantro over the top of the corn mixture and serve hot.",
    "Serve immediately and enjoy!"
  ],
